            "SIGN-IN COMMANDS": "أوامر تسجيل الدخول",
            "Save changes": "حفظ التغييرات",
            "Show the assistant, a chat in the corner of the window": "",
            "Shows, in the right-click menu, the actions that change a cluster: delete or evict a Pod, scale or restart a Deployment. Each one asks for confirmation. It also shows the kubectl command to open a shell in a Pod. Off keeps the app read-only.": "يعرض في قائمة النقر الأيمن الإجراءات التي تغيّر الكتلة: حذف Pod أو إخلاءه (evict)، تغيير حجم Deployment أو إعادة تشغيله. يطلب كل إجراء تأكيدًا. ويعرض أيضًا أمر kubectl لفتح shell في Pod. عند الإيقاف يبقى التطبيق للقراءة فقط.",
            "The assistant uses the client that is already installed on this computer, such as Claude Code or Codex, signed in the way you already are. KubeScope asks you for no credentials and stores none: the sign-in stays with that program. What you ask, attach and what it reads from the cluster go to that program and to its service. The conversations are kept on this computer, without the documents and logs that were read.": "",
